  - [1mBase URL per environment[0m — settings holds [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m, and callers compose [38;5;153m${apiBaseUrl}/login[39m. Buys: a second
    endpoint costs nothing later; environment switching stays one value per environment. Costs: one small indirection at
    each call site, and a trailing-slash convention to keep straight.
  - [1mFull endpoint URLs per environment[0m — settings holds a named map like [38;5;153mendpoints.login[39m. Buys: call sites read
    literally, no string building; endpoints can diverge across hosts. Costs: every new endpoint must be added for every
    environment, so the table grows N×M.

  I recommend the base URL. It's the smaller table, it's what "easier to change environments" actually asks for — one
  value to point at a different backend — and a named-endpoints layer can be added on top later without changing how
  environments are selected.

