[38;5;246m  ⎿  · What should settings store per environment? → Base URL (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m [1mFourth question: which environments do you need, and what maps to them?[0m

  I don't know your infrastructure, so I'll need the real values from you — but the set matters first, since it fixes
  the table's rows and the hostname mapping.

  For the values themselves: I'll fill in [38;5;153mlocalhost[39m → [38;5;153mhttp://localhost:3000[39m and keep [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com[39m as
  production so today's behavior is preserved exactly, and mark any staging host as a placeholder for you to correct in
  the spec. Unknown hostnames will fall back to production rather than failing — that's the safe default for a page
  served from a host nobody anticipated, though I'll flag it in the design since the opposite choice (fail loudly) is
  defensible too.
